			<div class="content" id="post-content-1469115">
									

<p>Okay, some thoughts.</p>
<p>1. For a first time, this is actually a remarkably original idea. Kudos for that.<br />
2. Your principal problem is a lack of clinical tone. It's really not a thing you can teach someone, but phrases like</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The team sent to observe the prisoners discovered a large amount of decomposing [DATA REDACTED] with SCP-1227 having formed in the center of it, seemingly in good physical and mental health, <strong>greeting the researchers like old friends.</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>The practical upshot of this is that SCP-1227 is now perfectly adapted to survive on limited resources.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The problem with the first is the bolded part; you effectively never need similes in SCPs, since researchers won't be comparing things to other things nonliterally. The whole tone of the second one (and a frequent tonal issue throughout the SCP) is that it sounds like a sidenote that a researcher wrote about the SCP; it uses terms that scientists would <em>never</em> use (&quot;upshot,&quot; &quot;perfectly adapted&quot;) and essentially sounds like it's praising the SCP for being a <em>good</em> SCP. Who's a good SCP? <em>SCP-1227</em>'s a good SCP! Yes you are!</p>
<p>3. The last addendum goes way too far. You were fine with what you had, before you added in &quot;BTW OMG ITS GONNA HAVE SCP BABIES ITS SPIDERS HE'S TALKING ABOUT MIDWIVES WHAT????&quot; Though I compliment you for not naming the kid &quot;Redips.&quot;</p>
<p>4. You might want to tone down the redactions. <a href="/zen-and-the-art-of-data-redacted">Here's</a> a guide on when not to redact; that whole addendum that is <em>just</em> a redaction should probably go ASAP. It tells us nothing and turns an otherwise serious article into lolfoundation.</p>
<p>5. The picture? What is that? It looks like it's from a movie, which may or may not be a problem of itself, but it's sort of a problem that it <em>looks</em> like it's from a movie. Is there any other picture you can get?</p>

