<p>I really like this article, the psychoanalysis bits really add to it.</p>
<p>A few minor annoyances on the biology angle:<br />
1) the reason we piss out so much water is nothing to do with in efficiencies in our internal organs: quite the opposite in fact! Essentially it’s a quick way to get rid of water in the blood, along with all the other nastiness you find in urea. I mean at a stretch you could have one of the bodies hold a stomach into which excess water is placed, but seems a bit odd.<br />
2) extra organs wouldn’t lead to extra respirational efficacy. what you want there is altered cell composition<br />
3)this can prolly be over looked, but muscles and esophagus need to be covered by skin, or some sort of impermeable membrane. they leak all over the carpet and make a mess other wise<br />
But yeah apart from those pedantic picks, seems damn fine!</p>

